<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chlodomer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 495–524</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Chlodomer of Orléans, Clodomir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chlodomer was a Frankish king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty">Merovingian dynasty</a>, the second son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> and Clotilde. When his father's realm was divided in 511 he received lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>. He was killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vezeronce">Battle of Vézeronce</a> in 524, after which his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> murdered two of his young sons and divided his kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chlodomer.jpg" alt="Chlodomer" width="269" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: schiesser philippe, Eric Vandenbossche · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chlodomer_denarius.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
